1
00:00:00,420 --> 00:00:08,433
In the Encyclopedia of Triangle Centers, the Complement and Anticomplement are the two universal homothety operators centered at the Centroid X two.

2
00:00:08,433 --> 00:00:16,770
Because the centroid divides every median in a two-to-one ratio, dilation through X two by negative one-half maps triangle A B C onto its medial triangle.

3
00:00:17,190 --> 00:00:28,447
For any center P, its complement lies on line P X two on the opposite side of X two at half the distance, with barycentric coordinates v plus w, w plus u, u plus v.

4
00:00:28,447 --> 00:00:38,880
Its anticomplement lies at twice the distance in the opposite direction, with barycentrics negative u plus v plus w, u minus v plus w, u plus v minus w.

5
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:56,780
This single homothety organizes two of the most famous lines in Collection One: on the Euler line, X five is the complement of X three and X four is the anticomplement of X three; on the Nagel line, Spieker center X ten is the complement of Incenter X one and Nagel point X eight is its anticomplement.
